// The call-site intrinsics are reserved words: `addr`, `drop`, `panic`, `assert`, `debugAssert` cannot name
// a function, a local, a parameter or a field. Before, `fn void assert(bool cond, string msg)` was accepted
// and silently never called (every bare `assert` lowered to the trap); a reserved word makes that
// unwritable, and the diagnostic says the word is reserved rather than naming a bare token.
fn void assert(bool cond, string msg) { }

fn int32 main() {
    return 0;
}
